    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #328\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nBranch `bb/relay-123-mcp-integration-01-07-store-mcp-server-thr_t6bh922k8p` pushed to origin successfully.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #123: seeds a Semprec-owned `mcpServers` system database and wires it into the propose/confirm flow so a human can attach credentials without ever exposing them to the AI-authored proposal path.\n\n- **New system database** `mcpServers` (`seedMcpModule.ts`): `name`, `connectionConfig` (strict `stdio`/`sse`/`http`-discriminated JSON schema in `mcp/mcpConnectionConfig.ts`), `active`, plus system-owned `syncStatus`/`lastSynced`. Seeded via a dedicated \"MCP\" project item, following the existing `seedEmailModule` pattern, wired into `seedSystem.ts`.\n- **Proposal validation** (`mcp/mcpServerProposal.ts`, hooked into `assertValidProposalEnvelope`): rejects any credential-shaped field (`credential`, `apiKey`, `token`, `secret`, `password`, etc.) outright, and enforces `connectionConfig` strictness for any proposal targeting `mcpServers`.\n- **Credential attachment on confirm** (`proposalActions.ts`): `confirmProposalWithClient` gained an optional `credential` parameter — a human-supplied secret stored via the existing `external_credentials` store in the same transaction as the item creation (atomic: either both persist or neither does), and rejected for any non-`mcpServers` target.\n- `syncStatus`/`lastSynced` are `owner: 'system'`, which structurally blocks both the proposal path and any future agent path from touching them or triggering a sync — no MCP-specific sync-blocking code needed (sync itself is out of scope, deferred to issue #125).\n\n**Verification performed this session:**\n- New integration suite `mcpServerProposal.test.ts` (12 tests): seed shape, config validation, credential-field rejection, atomic confirm-with-credential, confirm-without-credential, and confirm-refuses-credential-for-wrong-target (with rollback verified).\n- Full `pnpm run test` (unit + integration + e2e): 467 integration tests + 5 e2e tests + unit tests, all passing, including the pre-existing `proposalActions.test.ts` regression suite and a required update to `smoke.test.ts`'s exact seeded-database-name list.\n- `pnpm -r run build` (all 9 workspace packages) and `tsc --noEmit`: clean.\n- `pnpm run check:boundaries` (dependency-cruiser): no violations.\n\nNo plaintext credential is ever stored in item properties, proposal history, or logs.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
