    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #328\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch **`bb/relay-123-mcp-integration-01-07-store-mcp-server-thr_t6bh922k8p`** (`3a18988..7a07f85`).\n\nThis push adds the fix for the medium-severity review finding on PR #328: `assertValidMcpServerProposalProperties` now also rejects credential-shaped keys inside a `stdio` transport's `connectionConfig.env` map (normalized to catch `apiKey`, `API_KEY`, `api-key`, etc.), closing the smuggling gap where a secret could bypass the top-level denylist and land in `items.properties` instead of the encrypted `external_credentials` store. Three new tests cover this: rejecting `env.apiKey`, rejecting `env.API_KEY`, and accepting a benign `env.LOG_LEVEL`.\n\nVerified before push: full `pnpm run test` (unit + integration + e2e) passes with exit code 0, `pnpm -r run build` compiles clean across all 11 backend workspace packages, and `pnpm run check:boundaries` reports no dependency violations.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
