    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #328\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch **`bb/relay-123-mcp-integration-01-07-store-mcp-server-thr_t6bh922k8p`** (`7a07f85..bf84da3`).\n\nThis push adds the fix for the latest medium-severity review finding on PR #328: `sse`/`http` transport `connectionConfig.url` query-string parameters were not checked against the credential-field denylist, letting a secret smuggled as a URL query param (e.g. `?token=sk-...`) bypass both the top-level property check and the Zod schema and land in plaintext in `items.properties`. Added `assertNoCredentialShapedUrlParams` (`backend/packages/data/src/mcp/mcpServerProposal.ts`), which parses the URL and checks each query-param name against the same normalized denylist already used for `stdio`'s `env` map, with three new tests covering the rejection, its normalized-case variant, and a benign param passing through untouched.\n\nVerified before push: full `pnpm run test` (unit + integration + e2e) passes with exit code 0, `pnpm -r run build` compiles clean across all 11 backend workspace packages, and `pnpm run check:boundaries` reports no dependency violations.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
